(Regression test: FileSeekLine, FileSeekByte, and FileReadLine codegen
never set _last_error after calls, so 'On error' silently never fired
even on genuine failures.)

open a file for writing called setup at "/tmp/vox_test_seek_readline.txt".
Write "hello\nworld\n" to setup.
Close setup.

(SeekLine error: line 0 is invalid (1-indexed))
open a file for reading called f1 at "/tmp/vox_test_seek_readline.txt".
Seek f1 to line 0.
On error print "seek line error caught".
Close f1.

(SeekLine success: must not fire On error)
open a file for reading called f2 at "/tmp/vox_test_seek_readline.txt".
Seek f2 to line 2.
On error print "BUG: seek line 2 fired error", exit 1.
Print "seek line 2 ok".
a buffer called b1 is 32 bytes in size.
Read line from f2 into b1.
On error print "BUG: readline fired error", exit 1.
Print b1.
Close f2.

(SeekByte success: must not fire On error)
open a file for reading called f3 at "/tmp/vox_test_seek_readline.txt".
Seek f3 to byte 7.
On error print "BUG: seek byte 7 fired error", exit 1.
Print "seek byte 7 ok".
Close f3.

Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_seek_readline.txt".
